## Hints for Future Agents
Two distinct auto-compact knobs exist and they are easy to confuse:

  CLAUDE_AUTOCOMPACT_PCT_OVERRIDE   - percentage of window, BROKEN
  CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW   - absolute tokens, works

The percentage one has open bugs #52390, #63186, #70477, and #82761. #82761 is
filed against claude-opus-5[1m] specifically and reports it silently stopped
working after v2.1.220. Do not reach for it.

The env var only accepts a plain integer. "400k" will not parse. Range is
100000 to 1000000.

Actual compaction fires around 380000, not 400000. The bundle computes
  o - Math.min(sbr(e), lZu)   where lZu = 20000
so it reserves output-token budget capped at 20000. If the user ever complains
the number is off by ~20k, this is why, and it is not a bug.

Corollary worth remembering: because that reservation saturates at 20000,
CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=128000 does NOT cost context before compaction.
min(128000,20000) == min(64000,20000). The docs' general caveat that raising
output tokens shrinks the effective context window is true in principle but
already saturated at the model default, so it does not compound. It still
raises the real output cap, so it is not dead weight.

Live risk not resolved: #85031 reports auto-compact simply not firing on
Opus 5 near the top of a 1M window. That sits downstream of whatever window
value resolves, so this setting does not immunize against it. If compaction
stops happening entirely, suspect that before suspecting the config.

Also #78318: switching models mid-session with /model leaves the window stale
until restart.

## Codebase Discoveries
The resolver is Nq(e,t,r) in the bundle. Precedence, highest first: the env
var, then the autoCompactWindow settings key, then a model-tuned default of
500000. The env var was chosen over the settings key for that reason, and
because this file already keeps its knobs in the env block.

hC(e,r) resolves the raw model window. It tests the model string with a
literal /\[1m\]/i, so "opus[1m]" gets 1000000. Per issue #74562, sonnet[1m]
and fable[1m] do NOT currently receive the 1M window - only opus[1m] does.

On the three removals: CLAUDE_CODE_WORKFLOWS is read by nw_(), but the truthy
branch and the unset branch both fall through to the same tengu_workflows_enabled
gate, which itself defaults true. It only changes behavior when set falsy. The
supported way to turn workflows off is CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_WORKFLOWS or the
disableWorkflows key. CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ADAPTIVE_THINKING is ANDed with
f.includes("opus-4-6") || f.includes("sonnet-4-6"), so it is inert on
everything this config points at.

